<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Uraiyur</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Uraiyur was the inland capital of the early <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chola-empire">Chola</a> kings in the Sangam age, now a district of the city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tiruchirappalli">Tiruchirappalli</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tamil-nadu">Tamil Nadu</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>. Sangam poems describe it as a fortified city, and it was known for its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cotton">cotton</a> cloth. After the decline of the early Cholas it remained a local centre, and it was sacked by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pandya-dynasty">Pandyas</a> in the 13th century.</p></div>
